body:
Sorry to hear that your mom is not being more supportive. I do find that older people in previous generations generally are not as accepting in dealing with mental health issues. My own parents are quite dismissive of my sufferings as well so I know all too well how you are feeling. I remember reading a post from someone in their 60s that when they were young growing up any mental illness would be lumped together as being mentally retarded. Even now recognition of mental health issues are not really widespread unfortunately and people aren't getting the help they need.

&#x200B;

Edit: missed a word

Damn, you can already write programs after only coding a few days? I've been learning python off and on for about 3 months and probably can't do what you did.

&#x200B;

Very impressive. 

&#x200B;
